<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Parakramabahu VI</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">r. <a href="/years/1412">1412</a>–<a href="/years/1467">1467</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/15th-century">15th century</a> · Also known as Parakramabahu VI of Kotte</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Parakramabahu VI was the last Sinhalese king to unify all of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sri-lanka">Sri Lanka</a>. Rising to power at Gampola and ruling from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sri-jayawardenepura-kotte">Kotte</a> from 1412, he sent his adopted son to conquer the Tamil kingdom of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jaffna">Jaffna</a> and brought the hill country under control. His long reign was a high point of Sinhala literature, but the kingdom divided soon after his death in 1467.</p></div>
